---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../lib/site';
---
<Layout
  title="DigUp Release Notes Summary — 0.6.1 & 0.7 Beta"
  description="Plain-English summary of DigUp 0.6.1 Mac fixes and 0.7.0-beta.2 Windows/Linux updates."
  canonicalPath="/changelog-notes/"
  lang="en"
>
  <main class="wrap">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <p class="meta-line"><span class="badge">Summary</span></p>
      <h1>DigUp changelog notes</h1>
      <p class="lead">Condensed highlights for DigUp 0.6.1 (Mac) and 0.7.0-beta.2 (Windows/Linux). Versions cited were current on 2026-10-19. Based on DigUp (MIT).</p>
    </header>

    <article class="wide">
      <div class="cta-bar">
        <a class="cta" href={SITE.downloads.mac} rel="noopener noreferrer" download>Download DigUp for Mac</a>
        <a class="cta-secondary" href={SITE.downloads.windows} rel="noopener noreferrer" download>Windows</a>
        <a class="cta-secondary" href="/install-mac/">Mac install</a>
        <a class="cta-secondary" href="/install-windows/">Windows install</a>
      </div>

      <h2>0.6.1 — Mac (stable)</h2>
      <p class="muted">Tag <code>v0.6.1</code> · asset <code>DigUp-0.6.1.dmg</code> · Apple Silicon, macOS 14+</p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Area</th><th>What changed (summary)</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>IME</strong></td><td>Composed text (Korean/Japanese/Chinese) no longer breaks into loose letters in search.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Partial words</strong></td><td>Prefix matches (e.g. “Grok” in “Grok4”) stay found after you stop typing.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Folder names</strong></td><td>Accents / CJK in folder paths no longer halt indexing for every folder.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Indexing stability</strong></td><td>Fewer restart loops on huge changing folders; runaway file readers are skipped; helper memory growth on long text fixed.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Scanned PDFs</strong></td><td>OCR on scanned PDF pages (like screenshots) so typed invoice numbers can hit.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>SVG</strong></td><td>SVG images are indexed (were skipped).</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Scheduled hours</strong></td><td>Index only at set hours (default overnight window); search still works all day.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Offline model</strong></td><td><strong>Use Files…</strong> when network blocks the model download.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>Full install steps: <a href="/install-mac/">Install DigUp on Mac</a>. Mac is not in the 0.7.0-beta.2 train; next Mac release will carry the code-search security fix.</p>

      <h2>0.7.0-beta.2 — Windows &amp; Linux (beta)</h2>
      <p class="muted">Tag <code>v0.7.0-beta.2</code> · published 2026-10-18 · Mac remains on 0.6.1 · follows first beta (<code>v0.7.0-beta.1</code>, 2026-10-14)</p>
      <p>Fixes what people hit in beta.1 on Windows and Linux, plus three security hardening items. From this version, Windows and Linux update tracks are separate.</p>

      <h3>Stability fixes</h3>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><strong>Windows — 2–4&nbsp;GB file index stall:</strong> a single file between 2 and 4&nbsp;GB in a chosen folder stopped indexing before it started, so that folder and folders after it never got indexed. Fixed (upstream #87 / #100).</li>
        <li><strong>Linux AppImage — GStreamer hang:</strong> the search panel no longer freezes when a recording ranks first. The AppImage was missing GStreamer plugins WebKit needs (upstream #64).</li>
        <li><strong>Linux — model download resume:</strong> on some distros (Debian 13, Ubuntu 26.04 among them), the model download stopped after each finished file and DigUp had to be reopened. It now finishes in one go; if a download ends silently, DigUp re-checks files before calling it failed (upstream #64, #92).</li>
        <li><strong>Linux — indexing helper exit:</strong> the helper no longer stays in the background until DigUp quits (upstream #63).</li>
        <li><strong>Linux — AppImage login entry:</strong> extracted AppImage login entries now run AppRun instead of crashing at login (upstream #125).</li>
        <li><strong>Preview / file robustness:</strong> stop-words no longer highlight as matches; preview jumps to real hits. Malformed RTF or damaged HEIF is skipped instead of killing the helper.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Security</h3>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><strong>Code search / git config:</strong> listing a repo no longer lets that folder’s own git configuration run a program. Unzipped or copied project folders could carry such a config; normal clones were never affected, and code search stays off unless you enable it.</li>
        <li><strong>Crafted HEIF / zip bomb:</strong> a crafted HEIF photo, or a document with a zip entry claiming gigabytes, could stop the indexing helper on Linux and Windows — hardened.</li>
        <li>Advisories follow upstream; Mac will pick up the code-search fix in its next release.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>New</h3>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>Settings → General → <strong>“Run the model on the processor”</strong> for machines whose GPU returns empty or wrong results (upstream #97).</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Downloads</h3>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><strong>Windows:</strong> <a href={SITE.downloads.windows} rel="noopener noreferrer" download><code>DigUp_0.7.0-beta.2_x64-setup.exe</code></a> — 64-bit Windows 10/11, per-user, unsigned → SmartScreen More info → Run anyway. Windows installer / AppImage self-update from beta.1.</li>
        <li><strong>Linux:</strong> <a href={SITE.downloads.linuxDeb} rel="noopener noreferrer" download><code>DigUp_0.7.0-beta.2_amd64.deb</code></a> (package <code>dig-up</code>) or <a href={SITE.downloads.linuxAppImage} rel="noopener noreferrer" download><code>DigUp_0.7.0-beta.2_amd64.AppImage</code></a>; <code>chmod +x</code> for AppImage. Reinstall .deb over beta.1.</li>
        <li><strong>Hotkey:</strong> Ctrl+Shift+Space; Wayland GNOME/KDE can register it; other desktops bind manually.</li>
        <li><strong>Still not in this beta:</strong> screenshot OCR text; skip .doc / RAW / SVG on Win/Linux beta.</li>
      </ul>
      <ol class="checklist">
        <li>Follow <a href="/install-windows/">Windows</a> or <a href="/install-linux/">Linux</a> checklists.</li>
        <li>Report issues upstream with the <code>speed.log</code> device line when GPU behavior matters.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Version matrix (2026-10-19)</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Platform</th><th>Version</th><th>Channel</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>macOS</td><td>0.6.1</td><td>Stable</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Windows</td><td>0.7.0-beta.2</td><td>Beta</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Linux</td><td>0.7.0-beta.2</td><td>Beta</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="cta-bar">
        <a class="cta" href="/#download">All downloads</a>
        <a class="cta-secondary" href="/faq/">FAQ</a>
        <a class="cta-secondary" href="/zh/changelog-notes/" hreflang="zh-CN">中文更新说明</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
